        {
          "text": "WÊN T'ing-shih 文廷式 (T. 道希[溪], H. 芸閣, 純常子), 1856–1904, official and scholar, was a native of P'ing-hsiang, Kiangsi. After becoming a chü-jên, early in the eighteen-eighties, he went to Peking where he became acquainted with many prominent contemporaries, among them Shêng-yü [q. v.] who assisted him greatly.",
